    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538-a14">

                <pb facs="0893" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg757"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 14 in No. 973.—Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blacklock to Mr. Rives.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Apia, Samoa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-09-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 14, 1888</date>. (Received October 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 151.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The existing state of affairs here makes it
                    necessary to have the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Adams</hi> take
                    supplementary dispatches to the mail-steamer. I have the honor to inclose
                    herewith a record of current events since the regular mail left here on the 11th
                    instant. I inclose also a translation of a letter just received.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Blacklock</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">U. S. Vice-Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
